	"descriptionMarkdown": "Self-starting hybrid steam power plant with a dedicated solar and accumulator backup network.\n\nThe steam section provides the main power output, while the isolated solar network powers only the boiler fuel inserters. This allows the plant to automatically recover from a complete steam-grid blackout because the inserters remain powered and can continue feeding fuel into the boilers.\n\nThe roboports are intentionally excluded from the solar backup network and are powered only by the steam grid. This prevents roboport charging and logistics activity from draining the emergency accumulators.\n\nIncludes:\n\n* 96 steam engines\n* 48 boilers\n* 48 solar-powered boiler inserters\n* 208 solar panels\n* 173 accumulators\n* 6 steam-powered roboports\n* Balanced solar-to-accumulator ratio\n* Isolated emergency power network\n* Automatic black-start capability\n* Fixed compact footprint\n",
